If there's a shop with a potion of oil in it, and you light it, you get
charged for usage, and the price of the item, but if you can only
afford the usage fee, you can drop the potion (still lit), and sell it
back to the shopkeeper. You can then pick it up again, snuff it, and
sell it again. With ~12 Charisma, you lose 50 each time (for the usage
fee), but with really high charisma (18, for example), you can make 50
zorkmids each time.

So yeah, not proper behaviour.



